features/sea-compact/decisions.md-6-
features/sea-compact/decisions.md-7-- The operator's playtest verdict: the online duel "works and it's good, can be smoother", so the combat spike passes and duel smoothness is tuned later. On the sea: "have a denser map and reduce the scale". This feature does that before `encounters-theft`, because encounters need ships that meet, and encounter tests depend on map distances.
features/sea-compact/decisions.md-8-- §3's travel times stay binding (neighbours 20–40 s, longest crossing ≤ 90 s). Shrinking the world is only legal if ships slow down, so full speed drops from 5 to 3 tiles a second, and the map shrinks to at most 112 × 112 tiles (under a quarter of today's area).
features/sea-compact/decisions.md-9-- Corrected after design challenge attempt 1. The tile's 256 sub-units, the 64 headings and `turnRate` 1 stay unchanged: 1 is already the minimum, and the claim tests depend on 256. So full speed is 39 sub-units per step (3.05 tiles/s), and handling is judged on screen: time to full speed, stopping distance, 3.2 s per full turn, and the turning circle in pixels.
features/sea-compact/decisions.md-10-- "Ships meet" becomes a check, not a hope: every neighbour route passes within sight of one central `hub` point, because shoals block the direct routes along the edges. At about 3 tiles/s, the detour through the centre also keeps neighbours inside §3's 20–40 s.
features/sea-compact/decisions.md-11-- "Reduce the scale" also means drawing larger. Tiles go from 16 to about 24 px, so the 10-tile sight circle fits on the 800 × 560 view and on-screen speed stays about the same (80 → 72 px/s). The sight radius itself stays 10 tiles.
features/sea-compact/decisions.md-12-- Density is a validator, not a judgement: no navigable tile may be farther than the sight radius from a non-sea tile, and routes are funnelled through channels. This follows §3 ("Remove empty stretches before adding more sailing mechanics"), so there are no new mechanics (slow zones, currents).
features/sea-compact/decisions.md-13-- Still four small islands (§18 stage 2). A `rock` tile type for outcrops and landmarks is optional; shoals alone are acceptable.
features/sea-compact/decisions.md:14:- The flaky `sail-and-dock` browser test (seen in duel-online-fixes-001's worker phase) is fixed here, since this feature rewrites its route anyway: the test brakes until the dock hint reads "Press E to dock", then taps E, and it must pass 5 repeats.
features/sea-compact/decisions.md-15-- One fullstack lane (`world`) with all five checks and all six browser scenario ids. The owned paths list the sea files one by one, so the assistant's parallel ledger and claim fixes (`packages/*/src/objectives`, `packages/*/src/claim`) stay disjoint.
features/sea-compact/decisions.md-16-- Every acceptance item names its test, because most earlier blocked reviews came from acceptance items without one.
